{
  "version": "2b1",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "The dot product measures how much one vector points along another. For a nonzero vector b, project a onto the line through b. Then a · b is the signed length of that projection multiplied by the length of b: a · b = |a||b| cos θ, where θ is the angle between the vectors."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "The dot product is positive if the projection points along b and negative if it points opposite b. The length itself is never negative; the sign records direction. If a and b are orthogonal (at 90°), the projection lands at the origin, so the dot product is zero. It is also zero if either vector is the zero vector."
    },
    {
      "type": "ui",
      "source": "root = Stack([projectionDiagram])\nprojectionDiagram = Graphic(\"Negative and zero projections\", [{kind:\"text\",x:20,y:20,text:\"Negative projection\"},{kind:\"path\",d:\"M 105 91 L 46 43 M 46 43 L 56 45 M 46 43 L 50 53\"},{kind:\"path\",d:\"M 105 91 H 190 M 190 91 L 182 86 M 190 91 L 182 96\"},{kind:\"path\",d:\"M 46 50 V 56 M 46 61 V 67 M 46 72 V 78 M 46 83 V 88\"},{kind:\"path\",d:\"M 105 91 H 46 M 46 91 L 54 86 M 46 91 L 54 96\"},{kind:\"circle\",cx:105,cy:91,r:3},{kind:\"text\",x:32,y:44,text:\"a\"},{kind:\"text\",x:196,y:96,text:\"b\"},{kind:\"text\",x:20,y:119,text:\"Projection points left\"},{kind:\"text\",x:245,y:20,text:\"Orthogonal vectors\"},{kind:\"path\",d:\"M 267 91 V 43 M 267 43 L 262 51 M 267 43 L 272 51\"},{kind:\"path\",d:\"M 267 91 H 392 M 392 91 L 384 86 M 392 91 L 384 96\"},{kind:\"path\",d:\"M 267 79 H 279 V 91\"},{kind:\"circle\",cx:267,cy:91,r:3},{kind:\"text\",x:252,y:45,text:\"a\"},{kind:\"text\",x:398,y:96,text:\"b\"},{kind:\"text\",x:245,y:119,text:\"Projection is zero\"}])",
      "state": []
    }
  ]
}

