{
  "version": "2b1",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Decouple the three by separating durable facts, per-request decisions, and workflow. The Conversation Engine records what happened. The Context Engine decides what fits in this request. The Application Orchestrator decides when to call each one."
    },
    {
      "type": "ui",
      "source": "{\"root\":\"layout\",\"elements\":{\"layout\":{\"type\":\"Stack\",\"props\":{},\"children\":[\"dependencies\"]},\"dependencies\":{\"type\":\"Graphic\",\"props\":{\"label\":\"The orchestrator calls both engines; neither engine calls the other.\",\"items\":[{\"kind\":\"rect\",\"x\":127,\"y\":5,\"width\":196,\"height\":34},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"x\":143,\"y\":27,\"text\":\"Application Orchestrator\"},{\"kind\":\"path\",\"d\":\"M 225 39 V 56 H 110 V 78 M 104 72 L 110 78 L 116 72 M 225 56 H 340 V 78 M 334 72 L 340 78 L 346 72\"},{\"kind\":\"rect\",\"x\":13,\"y\":80,\"width\":194,\"height\":44},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"x\":31,\"y\":107,\"text\":\"Conversation Engine\"},{\"kind\":\"rect\",\"x\":243,\"y\":80,\"width\":194,\"height\":44},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"x\":284,\"y\":107,\"text\":\"Context Engine\"}]}}}}",
      "state": []
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Conversation Engine — Own messages, parent links, and branch heads. Expose a read that returns a stable snapshot at a named head, and an append that takes an explicit parent. When advancing an existing branch, check the expected head so a stale request cannot silently attach its reply to a different turn."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Context Engine — Take a read-only conversation snapshot, a reference scope, and an input budget in tokens. Return selected references in prompt order, with source IDs and token counts. Keep ranking and truncation policy here. A reference included for one request does not become a conversation message."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Application Orchestrator — Append the user turn, read the branch at that message, and reserve room for fixed prompt content and model output before passing the remaining input budget to the Context Engine. Assemble the request, call the model, and append the reply to the user turn it answered. Use an idempotency key for appends so retries do not duplicate turns."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Keep the handoffs to IDs, snapshots, and explicit budgets, not shared tables. That lets you change reference ranking without migrating conversation history, and change retry behavior without modifying either engine."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "version": "2b1",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "The dot product measures how much one vector points along another. For nonzero vectors a and b with angle θ between them, a · b = ‖a‖ ‖b‖ cos θ. The signed length of b’s projection onto a is ‖b‖ cos θ, so multiplying that signed length by ‖a‖ gives the dot product."
    },
    {
      "type": "ui",
      "source": "{\"root\":\"layout\",\"elements\":{\"layout\":{\"type\":\"Stack\",\"props\":{},\"children\":[\"projection\"]},\"projection\":{\"type\":\"Graphic\",\"props\":{\"label\":\"Positive, zero, and negative projections of b onto a\",\"items\":[{\"kind\":\"text\",\"x\":22,\"y\":19,\"text\":\"Positive\"},{\"kind\":\"path\",\"d\":\"M 12 96 H 139 M 131 92 L 139 96 L 131 100 M 49 96 L 105 41 M 96 44 L 105 41 L 102 50 M 105 49 V 57 M 105 63 V 71 M 105 77 V 85 M 105 91 V 96\"},{\"kind\":\"circle\",\"cx\":49,\"cy\":96,\"r\":3},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"x\":112,\"y\":43,\"text\":\"b\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"x\":129,\"y\":83,\"text\":\"a\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"x\":59,\"y\":119,\"text\":\"+ projection\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"x\":174,\"y\":19,\"text\":\"Orthogonal\"},{\"kind\":\"path\",\"d\":\"M 162 96 H 289 M 281 92 L 289 96 L 281 100 M 209 96 V 41 M 204 49 L 209 41 L 214 49 M 209 86 H 219 V 96\"},{\"kind\":\"circle\",\"cx\":209,\"cy\":96,\"r\":3},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"x\":219,\"y\":43,\"text\":\"b\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"x\":279,\"y\":83,\"text\":\"a\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"x\":164,\"y\":119,\"text\":\"Zero projection\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"x\":329,\"y\":19,\"text\":\"Negative\"},{\"kind\":\"path\",\"d\":\"M 312 96 H 439 M 431 92 L 439 96 L 431 100 M 389 96 L 333 41 M 336 50 L 333 41 L 342 44 M 333 49 V 57 M 333 63 V 71 M 333 77 V 85 M 333 91 V 96\"},{\"kind\":\"circle\",\"cx\":389,\"cy\":96,\"r\":3},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"x\":319,\"y\":43,\"text\":\"b\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"x\":429,\"y\":83,\"text\":\"a\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"x\":324,\"y\":119,\"text\":\"− projection\"}]}}}}",
      "state": []
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "In each panel, a points right from the dot. Drop a perpendicular from the tip of b to the line through a. If it lands to the right of the dot, the projection is positive. If a and b are orthogonal (90°), it lands at the dot, so the dot product is zero. If it lands to the left, the projection points opposite a, so its signed length—and the dot product—is negative. A dot product involving the zero vector is also zero, even though the angle is undefined."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "version": "2b1",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "The dot product measures how much one vector points along another. For nonzero vectors a and b with angle θ between them, a · b = ‖a‖‖b‖ cos θ. Drop a perpendicular from the tip of b to the line through a. The signed distance from the shared tail to that point is ‖b‖ cos θ. Multiply this signed projection by ‖a‖ to get the dot product."
    },
    {
      "type": "ui",
      "source": "{\"root\":\"layout\",\"elements\":{\"layout\":{\"type\":\"Stack\",\"props\":{},\"children\":[\"diagram\"]},\"diagram\":{\"type\":\"Graphic\",\"props\":{\"label\":\"Project b onto the line through a. The circle marks where the vertical perpendicular from b's tip meets the line.\",\"items\":[{\"kind\":\"text\",\"x\":16,\"y\":20,\"text\":\"Positive\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"x\":166,\"y\":20,\"text\":\"Orthogonal\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"x\":316,\"y\":20,\"text\":\"Negative\"},{\"kind\":\"path\",\"d\":\"M 16 99 H 133 M 166 99 H 283 M 316 99 H 433\"},{\"kind\":\"path\",\"d\":\"M 62 99 H 124 M 117 94 L 124 99 L 117 104 M 212 99 H 274 M 267 94 L 274 99 L 267 104 M 362 99 H 424 M 417 94 L 424 99 L 417 104\"},{\"kind\":\"path\",\"d\":\"M 62 99 L 97 49 M 89 52 L 97 49 L 97 58 M 212 99 V 49 M 207 56 L 212 49 L 217 56 M 362 99 L 327 49 M 327 58 L 327 49 L 335 52\"},{\"kind\":\"path\",\"d\":\"M 97 55 V 62 M 97 67 V 74 M 97 79 V 86 M 97 91 V 95 M 327 55 V 62 M 327 67 V 74 M 327 79 V 86 M 327 91 V 95\"},{\"kind\":\"circle\",\"cx\":97,\"cy\":99,\"r\":3},{\"kind\":\"circle\",\"cx\":212,\"cy\":99,\"r\":3},{\"kind\":\"circle\",\"cx\":327,\"cy\":99,\"r\":3},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"x\":113,\"y\":121,\"text\":\"a\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"x\":263,\"y\":121,\"text\":\"a\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"x\":413,\"y\":121,\"text\":\"a\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"x\":100,\"y\":45,\"text\":\"b\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"x\":220,\"y\":49,\"text\":\"b\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"x\":316,\"y\":44,\"text\":\"b\"}]}}}}",
      "state": []
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "For an acute angle, the projection lands ahead of the shared tail, in a’s direction, so the dot product is positive. At 90°, the vectors are orthogonal: the projection lands at the tail, so the dot product is zero. For an obtuse angle, the projection lands behind the tail, opposite a’s direction, so the dot product is negative. If either vector is zero, the dot product is zero even though the angle is undefined."
    }
  ]
}

