{
  "version": "2b1",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Separate the record of what happened from the decision about what to include next. The Conversation Engine owns the record, the Context Engine builds a budgeted input, and the Application Orchestrator runs the turn. Neither engine calls the other."
    },
    {
      "type": "ui",
      "source": "root = Stack([diagram])\ndiagram = Graphic(\"The orchestrator calls both engines\", [{kind:\"rect\",x:108,y:8,width:234,height:34},{kind:\"text\",x:130,y:30,text:\"Application Orchestrator\"},{kind:\"path\",d:\"M 225 42 V 59 H 110 V 81 M 105 75 L 110 81 L 115 75 M 225 59 H 340 V 81 M 335 75 L 340 81 L 345 75\"},{kind:\"rect\",x:12,y:82,width:196,height:40},{kind:\"text\",x:23,y:107,text:\"Conversation Engine\"},{kind:\"rect\",x:242,y:82,width:196,height:40},{kind:\"text\",x:281,y:107,text:\"Context Engine\"}])",
      "state": []
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Conversation Engine — Store messages and their parent links. Expose operations to append a message against an explicit parent and read a snapshot at a specific branch tip. It answers “What happened on this branch?” without deciding what belongs in a model prompt."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Context Engine — Given a read-only conversation snapshot, a reference query, and an input-token budget, select and fit the references. Return the selected content, source IDs, and token counts. Make omissions or an insufficient budget explicit; never rewrite messages or lineage to make the input fit."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Application Orchestrator — Append the user message, read the snapshot ending at that message, and call the Context Engine with the budget left after reserving space for fixed instructions and the model’s reply. Call the model, then append the reply to that same user message—not to whichever branch tip happens to be current."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Use immutable snapshots and stable IDs at the boundaries, not shared tables. Give message writes idempotency keys so a retried turn does not duplicate messages. If a run must be auditable, record its snapshot ID, selected reference versions, and budget separately from the conversation record."
    }
  ]
}

