{
  "version": "2b1",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Decouple the engines by giving each one a different decision: the Conversation Engine decides what happened in the conversation, the Context Engine decides what fits in the model’s input, and the Application Orchestrator decides what runs next."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Conversation Engine — Own messages and their lineage. Expose operations to append a message against an expected branch head and to read a snapshot at a specific head. Edits and regenerations create new lineage rather than silently changing an earlier snapshot. The engine does not rank references or call the model."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Context Engine — Take a conversation snapshot, candidate references, and an explicit input budget. Select and order references, then return a context package with source IDs, estimated token costs, and any budget shortfall. Budget against the target model’s tokenizer and account for required prompt content before adding optional references. If required content alone exceeds the budget, report that instead of silently dropping it. Context selection never rewrites the conversation."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Application Orchestrator — For each turn, append the user message, read the resulting snapshot, ask the Context Engine for a package, and call the model. Keep track of which snapshot and references the model saw. Append the reply against the head used for generation; if that head has moved, handle the conflict explicitly rather than attaching the reply to unseen history."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Use explicit request and response contracts, not shared mutable state. The orchestrator passes snapshot data and reference IDs between the engines; neither engine calls the other. That lets you change reference ranking without migrating conversation history, add branching without changing the ranking algorithm, and test each engine independently."
    }
  ]
}

