{
  "version": "2b1",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Decouple the three components by giving each a different decision: the Conversation Engine decides what happened in the conversation, the Context Engine decides what fits in the next model request, and the Application Orchestrator decides what happens next."
    },
    {
      "type": "ui",
      "source": "root = Stack([diagram])\ndiagram = Graphic(\"The orchestrator calls both engines; neither engine calls the other\", [{kind:\"rect\",x:106,y:8,width:238,height:30},{kind:\"text\",x:128,y:28,text:\"Application Orchestrator\"},{kind:\"path\",d:\"M 225 38 V 59 H 110 V 83 M 105 77 L 110 83 L 115 77 M 225 59 H 340 V 83 M 335 77 L 340 83 L 345 77\"},{kind:\"rect\",x:8,y:85,width:204,height:42},{kind:\"text\",x:28,y:102,text:\"Conversation Engine\"},{kind:\"text\",x:28,y:120,text:\"Messages and lineage\"},{kind:\"rect\",x:238,y:85,width:204,height:42},{kind:\"text\",x:258,y:102,text:\"Context Engine\"},{kind:\"text\",x:258,y:120,text:\"Selection and budget\"}])",
      "state": []
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Conversation Engine: append messages against explicit parent IDs and return a read-only snapshot of the selected branch. It owns IDs and lineage validation. It does not rank references, count prompt tokens, or call the model."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Context Engine: take the snapshot, candidate references, and the token budget available for references. Return the selected references in prompt order, with their source IDs and token usage. Measure cost using the tokenizer for the target model. If nothing fits, return an empty selection rather than exceeding the budget. It never writes messages or changes lineage."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Application Orchestrator: append the user message, read the branch snapshot at that message, and compute the reference budget after accounting for required prompt content and reserved response capacity. Ask the Context Engine for a selection, call the model, then append the reply to the original user message—not whichever message is newest when the model returns."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Use explicit request and response types rather than shared mutable state. Pass the snapshot into context selection instead of letting the Context Engine fetch live conversation state. Keep retries in the orchestrator and make appends idempotent so a retried turn does not create duplicate messages. That gives you three independent tests: lineage with fixed IDs, selection with fixed snapshots and budgets, and workflow with stubbed engines."
    }
  ]
}
